# Builds Caddy from source instead of using the published caddy image as-is.
#
# Reason: the published caddy:2.11.4 binary is built with Go 1.26.3, which carries
# CVE-2026-56862 (GO-2026-6090). A client can send post-handshake KeyUpdate messages to make the
# TLS server perform key derivation indefinitely. Caddy is the internet facing TLS terminator in
# this deployment, so that path is reachable by any unauthenticated client. The fix is in Go
# 1.25.13 / 1.26.6 / 1.27.0 and only a rebuild picks it up.
#
# The --replace lines lift dependencies that carry HIGH or CRITICAL findings: x/crypto
# (CVE-2026-56854, ssh source-address restrictions), x/net (DNS record parsing panic), x/text
# (norm.Iter infinite loop), grpc-go (xDS RBAC, HTTP/2 transport, CVE-2026-84304), go-jose v4
# (CVE-2026-116587, RSA JWK validation DoS) and klauspost/compress (CVE-2026-63209, s2 dictionary
# integer overflow). They are plain version bumps, so no per-CVE reachability judgement is needed.
#
# Every --replace is a hard override, not a floor: it holds the module at that exact version in
# both directions. That is why grpc sat on v1.82.1 after the CVE-2026-84304 fix shipped in
# v1.83.1, and why x/crypto is listed explicitly rather than left to minimal version selection,
# where a later change to the x/net pin could drop it back below v0.55.0. Re-read the whole list
# whenever one entry moves, and check compatibility rather than always taking the newest tag.
#
# CVE-2026-56854 affects every x/crypto below v0.55.0, so the v0.53.0 this image carried was not
# introduced by the x/net pin. The v0.52.0 Caddy asks for was affected just the same. Only the
# bump to v0.55.0 clears it.
#
# Go 1.27.2 and x/net v0.60.0 clear the October 2026 HTTP Range, HTTP/2 SETTINGS and TLS ECH
# findings (CVE-2026-78667, CVE-2026-78669, CVE-2026-97031). x/net v0.60.0 requires x/crypto
# v0.57.0 and x/text v0.42.0, so their hard overrides must move with it to avoid downgrading them.
#
# Go 1.27.3 clears CVE-2026-111943 (crypto/x509 stops returning chains through a set of distrusted
# intermediates). go-jose v4 and klauspost/compress had no --replace before; the v4.1.4 and v1.18.6
# that Caddy selects on its own are both affected, and v4.1.6 / v1.18.7 are the fixed releases.
#
# go-jose v3 carries the same CVE-2026-116587 with no fixed release, and caddypki links it through
# smallstep's go.step.sm/crypto, which still requires v3 in its newest release. No pin removes it,
# so it is accepted rather than fixed: security/trivy/web-writing-tool-caddy.trivyignore.yaml
# records why the vulnerable JWK parsing is unreachable in this deployment.
#
# apk upgrade in the runtime stage clears the c-ares and curl findings in the base layer.
# Docker caches that layer by its command text, so on a host that built it before, it keeps the
# packages that were current then: brotli CVE-2026-111497 and curl CVE-2026-92392 came back on
# 2026-10-28 from a layer cached on 2026-10-02. CI builds without a cache. A host that keeps one
# must rebuild only this stage with --no-cache-filter runtime, as wwt-seo-infra's
# build-and-scan-caddy.sh does, so keep the stage name in step with it.
#
# Exit condition: once an upstream caddy image is published that is built with
# Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3 or newer and carries no HIGH/CRITICAL findings other than the accepted
# go-jose v3 entry, delete this file and point docker-compose.yml back at the official image.
# docs/ci-cd-design.md records the check.

ARG CADDY_VERSION=2.11.4
ARG GO_VERSION=1.27.3
ARG XCADDY_VERSION=v0.4.7

FROM golang:${GO_VERSION}-alpine AS build

ARG CADDY_VERSION
ARG XCADDY_VERSION

# GOTOOLCHAIN=local keeps the build on the pinned Go version. Without it the toolchain directive
# in Caddy's go.mod can pull a different toolchain and silently undo the reason for this image.
ENV GOTOOLCHAIN=local \
    CGO_ENABLED=0

RUN apk add --no-cache git

RUN go install github.com/caddyserver/xcaddy/cmd/xcaddy@${XCADDY_VERSION}

RUN xcaddy build "v${CADDY_VERSION}" \
    --replace golang.org/x/crypto=golang.org/x/crypto@v0.57.0 \
    --replace golang.org/x/net=golang.org/x/net@v0.60.0 \
    --replace golang.org/x/text=golang.org/x/text@v0.42.0 \
    --replace google.golang.org/grpc=google.golang.org/grpc@v1.83.2 \
    --replace github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4=github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4@v4.1.6 \
    --replace github.com/klauspost/compress=github.com/klauspost/compress@v1.18.7 \
    --output /out/caddy

FROM caddy:${CADDY_VERSION} AS runtime

RUN apk --no-cache upgrade

COPY --from=build /out/caddy /usr/bin/caddy
